1. Basic Data Types 
- Integer: int, long, long long, short (distinguish between signed and unsigned). 
- Characters & Strings: Char characters, string strings (or char[] character arrays).
- Real numbers: float, double.
2. Basic Data Structures
- Array: Collection of consecutive elements of the same data type. 
- Linked List: Contains nodes connected to each other via addresses/pointers ending in NULL. 
- Stack & Queue: Special data retrieval methods (for example: first in, last out, first in first out).
3. Advanced Data Structures
- Tree: Branching structure in the form of nodes and branches
- Graph: Includes vertices and edges. Can be represented by an adjacent matrix or an adjacent list. 
- Hash Table: A combination of array and linked list along with hash function to store data.
